# Local verification (Cursor)

Governance entry: [`top/AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (repository root).

## Tooling assumption

This workspace is edited in **Cursor on a local machine** where `dotnet`, `deno`, and `docker` are installed and on `PATH`. CI runners also provide these tools.

- **Do** run checks directly: `dotnet test`, `deno test`, `bash .agent/tests/*.sh`.
- **Do not** report "tool not found" and stop without trying host commands.
- **Do not** use a Docker SDK image as a substitute for host `dotnet test` / `deno test` when local tools are available.
- Use Docker only when a script explicitly requires it (e.g. `.agent/tests/check-runtime-environment.sh`).

## Test output policy

Gate scripts under `.agent/tests/` follow [`.agent/tests/README.md`](../../.agent/tests/README.md): **short PASS on success**, **full runner replay on FAIL** via `.agent/scripts/lib/noise_control.sh`. Prefer `bash .agent/tests/check-*.sh` over raw `dotnet test` / `deno test` when verifying completion.

## Common commands

```bash
# Same as .github/workflows/runtime-semantics.yml
bash .agent/tests/check-runtime-semantics.sh

# Backend unit tests only
dotnet test backend/tests/Topolactor.Runtime.Tests/Topolactor.Runtime.Tests.csproj --nologo -v minimal

# Integration slice
dotnet test backend/tests/Topolactor.Integration.Tests/Topolactor.Integration.Tests.csproj --nologo -v minimal

# Frontend semantics slice (from check-runtime-semantics.sh)
deno test frontend/tests/adminApi.test.ts frontend/tests/defaultEntitySearch.test.ts frontend/tests/pipelineContinuity.test.ts --allow-read

# Full local CI (structure check runs last inside the script)
bash .agent/tests/check-local-ci.sh
```

